{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "<a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/inoue0426/llm-tuning-playground/blob/main/notebooks/05_grpo_drug_target_retrieval_local.ipynb\" target=\"_parent\"><img src=\"https://colab.research.google.com/assets/colab-badge.svg\" alt=\"Open In Colab\"/></a>\n",
        "\n",
        "# 05 - GRPO with a local drug-target verifier\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook uses a local copy of `drug_bank.csv` supplied by the user at runtime. The file is not stored in this public repository.\n",
        "\n",
        "The experiment builds a compact drug -> target dictionary, trains a small Qwen model with GRPO + LoRA, and evaluates exact target retrieval on unseen drugs.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Important:** keep any licensed or restricted source data outside this public repository and use it only according to its original terms."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!pip -q install -U \\\n",
        "    \"transformers>=4.55,<5\" \\\n",
        "    \"datasets>=3.6,<5\" \\\n        "    \"peft>=0.17,<1\" \\\n        "    \"trl>=0.29,<1\" \\\n        "    \"accelerate>=1.10,<2\" \\\n        "    \"bitsandbytes>=0.46,<1\" \\\n        "    \"torchao>=0.16,<1\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import ast\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import re\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import torch\n",
        "from datasets import Dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "import transformers, datasets, peft, trl\n",
        "print('PyTorch:', torch.__version__)\n",
        "print('Transformers:', transformers.__version__)\n",
        "print('Datasets:', datasets.__version__)\n",
        "print('PEFT:', peft.__version__)\n",
        "print('TRL:', trl.__version__)\n",
        "print('CUDA available:', torch.cuda.is_available())\n",
        "if not torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
        "    raise RuntimeError('Select a GPU runtime in Colab before running this notebook.')\n",
        "print('GPU:', torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))\n",
        "print('VRAM (GB):', round(torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).total_memory / 1024**3, 1))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Upload `drug_bank.csv` locally\n",
        "\n",
        "Put a local copy of the source file in the Colab runtime. Nothing is downloaded from or uploaded to GitHub.\n",
        "\n",
        "Expected file: `drug_bank.csv`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from google.colab import files\n",
        "\n",
        "uploaded = files.upload()\n",
        "\n",
        "if 'drug_bank.csv' not in uploaded:\n",
        "    raise FileNotFoundError('Please upload a file named drug_bank.csv')\n",
        "\n",
        "DATA_PATH = '/content/drug_bank.csv'\n",
        "print('Using:', DATA_PATH)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "df = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH)\n",
        "print('Rows:', len(df))\n",
        "print('Columns:', list(df.columns))\n",
        "df.head()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Build a compact one-target dictionary\n",
        "\n",
        "For the first GRPO experiment we keep only drugs with exactly one target in the source table. The reward checks the target UniProt ID exactly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "drug_targets = {}\n",
        "for _, row in df.iterrows():\n",
        "    drug = str(row['Drug Name']).strip()\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        target_ids = ast.literal_eval(str(row['Targets']))\n",
        "    except Exception:\n",
        "        target_ids = []\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        target_names = ast.literal_eval(str(row['Targets Name']))\n",
        "    except Exception:\n",
        "        target_names = []\n",
        "    pairs = list(zip(target_ids, target_names))\n",
        "    if drug and pairs:\n",
        "        drug_targets[drug] = pairs\n",
        "\n",
        "single_target = {d: pairs[0] for d, pairs in drug_targets.items() if len(pairs) == 1}\n",
        "print('Drugs with exactly one target:', len(single_target))\n",
        "print(list(single_target.items())[:10])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Create a prompt-only GRPO dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "The model receives only the prompt. The gold target is kept in another dataset column and passed to the reward function. We split by drug, so evaluation drugs are unseen during training."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "records = []\n",
        "for drug, (target_id, target_name) in single_target.items():\n",
        "    records.append({\n",
        "        'prompt': [\n",
        "            {'role': 'user', 'content': f'What is the protein target UniProt ID for the drug {drug}? Reply with the UniProt ID only.'}\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        'drug': drug,\n",
        "        'target_id': target_id,\n",
        "        'target_name': target_name,\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "dataset = Dataset.from_list(records).shuffle(seed=42)\n",
        "split = dataset.train_test_split(test_size=0.2, seed=42)\n",
        "train_dataset = split['train']\n",
        "eval_dataset = split['test']\n",
        "\n",
        "print('Total:', len(dataset))\n",
        "print('Train:', len(train_dataset))\n",
        "print('Eval:', len(eval_dataset))\n",
        "print(train_dataset[0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Load Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct\n",
        "\n",
        "We use the same small model as the earlier notebooks so the main change is the training objective and the verifiable reward."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoTokenizer\n",
        "\n",
        "MODEL_NAME = 'Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct'\n",
        "tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(MODEL_NAME)\n",
        "if tokenizer.pad_token is None:\n",
        "    tokenizer.pad_token = tokenizer.eos_token\n",
        "tokenizer.padding_side = 'left'\n",
        "\n",
        "dtype = torch.bfloat16 if torch.cuda.is_bf16_supported() else torch.float16\n",
        "model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(MODEL_NAME, torch_dtype=dtype).cuda()\n",
        "print('Has chat template:', tokenizer.chat_template is not None)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Before-GRPO evaluation\n",
        "\n",
        "We save exact-match accuracy on the held-out drugs before training. This gives a real before/after comparison."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def generate_answer(model, drug, max_new_tokens=16, do_sample=False):\n",
        "    messages = [{'role': 'user', 'content': f'What is the protein target UniProt ID for the drug {drug}? Reply with the UniProt ID only.'}]\n",
        "    encoded = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(\n",
        "        messages,\n",
        "        tokenize=True,\n",
        "        add_generation_prompt=True,\n",
        "        return_tensors='pt',\n",
        "        return_dict=True,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    encoded = {k: v.to(model.device) for k, v in encoded.items()}\n",
        "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
        "        output = model.generate(\n",
        "            **encoded,\n",
        "            max_new_tokens=max_new_tokens,\n",
        "            do_sample=do_sample,\n",
        "            pad_token_id=tokenizer.pad_token_id,\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    return tokenizer.decode(output[0], skip_special_tokens=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "def extract_target(text):\n",
        "    found = re.findall(r'\\b[A-Z][0-9][A-Z0-9]{3}[0-9]\\b', text.upper())\n",
        "    return found[0] if found else None\n",
        "\n",
        "def exact_accuracy(model, dataset):\n",
        "    correct = 0\n",
        "    rows = []\n",
        "    for ex in dataset:\n",
        "        text = generate_answer(model, ex['drug'])\n",
        "        pred = extract_target(text)\n",
        "        ok = pred == ex['target_id'].upper()\n",
        "        correct += int(ok)\n",
        "        rows.append((ex['drug'], ex['target_id'], pred, ok))\n",
        "    acc = correct / len(dataset) if len(dataset) else float('nan')\n",
        "    return acc, rows\n",
        "\n",
        "before_acc, before_rows = exact_accuracy(model, eval_dataset)\n",
        "print(f'Before GRPO exact target accuracy: {before_acc:.3f}')\n",
        "for drug, gold, pred, ok in before_rows[:10]:\n",
        "    print(f'{drug}: gold={gold}, pred={pred}, correct={ok}')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 6. Verifiable reward\n",
        "\n",
        "GRPO samples multiple completions and scores them with a reward function. Here the verifier is deterministic: reward 1 if the generated text contains the gold UniProt ID, otherwise 0."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def target_reward(completions, target_id, **kwargs):\n",
        "    rewards = []\n",
        "    for completion, gold in zip(completions, target_id):\n",
        "        text = completion[0]['content'] if isinstance(completion, list) else str(completion)\n",
        "        found = re.findall(r'\\b[A-Z][0-9][A-Z0-9]{3}[0-9]\\b', text.upper())\n",
        "        rewards.append(1.0 if str(gold).upper() in found else 0.0)\n",
        "    return rewards"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 7. GRPO + LoRA\n",
        "\n",
        "This is the core experiment: the model is not shown a chosen/rejected pair. It generates candidate answers and receives a verifier reward."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from peft import LoraConfig\n",
        "from trl import GRPOConfig, GRPOTrainer\n",
        "\n",
        "lora_config = LoraConfig(\n",
        "    r=8,\n",
        "    lora_alpha=16,\n",
        "    lora_dropout=0.05,\n",
        "    target_modules=['q_proj','k_proj','v_proj','o_proj'],\n",
        "    bias='none',\n",
        "    task_type='CAUSAL_LM',\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "grpo_args = GRPOConfig(\n",
        "    output_dir='./outputs/drug-target-grpo',\n",
        "    per_device_train_batch_size=2,\n",
        "    gradient_accumulation_steps=4,\n",
        "    learning_rate=5e-6,\n",
        "    max_steps=100,\n",
        "    num_generations=4,\n",
        "    max_prompt_length=128,\n",
        "    max_completion_length=16,\n",
        "    logging_steps=10,\n",
        "    save_strategy='no',\n",
        "    report_to='none',\n",
        "    use_vllm=False,\n",
        "    fp16=torch.cuda.is_available() and not torch.cuda.is_bf16_supported(),\n",
        "    bf16=torch.cuda.is_available() and torch.cuda.is_bf16_supported(),\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "trainer = GRPOTrainer(\n",
        "    model=model,\n",
        "    args=grpo_args,\n",
        "    train_dataset=train_dataset,\n",
        "    processing_class=tokenizer,\n",
        "    reward_funcs=target_reward,\n",
        "    peft_config=lora_config,\n",
        ")\n",
        "trainer.train()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 8. After-GRPO evaluation\n",
        "\n",
        "The evaluation set contains drugs not used during GRPO training. Exact matching keeps the reward and the final metric aligned."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "after_acc, after_rows = exact_accuracy(model, eval_dataset)\n",
        "print(f'After GRPO exact target accuracy: {after_acc:.3f}')\n",
        "for drug, gold, pred, ok in after_rows[:10]:\n",
        "    print(f'{drug}: gold={gold}, pred={pred}, correct={ok}')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 9. Before vs After\n",
        "\n",
        "This is the main result of the notebook."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print('Metric comparison')\n",
        "print(f'Base / before GRPO : {before_acc:.3f}')\n",
        "print(f'GRPO / after GRPO  : {after_acc:.3f}')\n",
        "print(f'Absolute gain      : {after_acc - before_acc:+.3f}')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## What this experiment demonstrates\n",
        "\n",
        "DPO learns from explicit preference pairs. GRPO instead optimizes against a reward verifier. Here the verifier is a deterministic drug-target lookup built from a local copy of `drug_bank.csv`.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is still a toy RL experiment. The one-target restriction and exact-match reward are deliberate simplifications. A stronger version should support multiple valid targets, hard negatives, entity normalization, and a public redistributable DTI benchmark for reproducibility."
      ]
    }
  ],
